Phase 1: Go-Live (March 2026)
Workflow Overview
Curebase will transmit a preferred appointment date/time to Portamedic using the Unscheduled Appointment Path (same approach currently used with Natera).
Portamedic will schedule appointments through their Traditional Scheduling workflow rather than Smart Scheduler.
Appointment confirmations updates will not be returned to Curebase during this phase.
Status updates will be a part of this.
Cost Alignment
This approach is fully covered under the previously scoped $5,000 per-2 timepoints setup fee for Portamedic.
The original budget assumes two timepoints, and this phase aligns with that model.

Phase 2: Looking ahead
We’re also exploring a potential Phase 2 that would introduce a more integrated scheduling workflow. We haven’t committed to this yet, as feasibility and timing will depend on where we land with the remaining integrations for this project (which it seems like we have most of our answers for now) and how this fits alongside other integration and engineering priorities within the Walgreens portfolio.
Enhanced Integration Workflow
Curebase will send actual appointment times to Portamedic based on Portamedic’s real-time availability (Scheduled Appointment Path).
If no availability exists, Curebase will transmit participant details without a time/date, following the Unscheduled Appointment Path.
Portamedic will identify these cases as non-Smart Scheduler and process them via their Traditional Scheduling workflow.
In this phase, confirmed appointment times and status updates will flow back into Curebase.
Revised Integration Estimate
Replace the previously optional $10,000 integration line item (“Portamedic Integration – may require work if Axle is being used”) with a revised estimate of $15,000, reflecting the need for new endpoints and materially different integration work than originally proposed.

